<%#
# The channel is closed for the clinic

Shown when a clinic comes back from Google or Microsoft to connect a mailbox while
the e-mail channel is closed for it (the platform switch «Каналы» or an exception of
the clinic). It is a plain page of its own: the operator app cannot show this reason.
The colours are the system ones, so the page follows the light or dark theme of the
browser.

## Instance variables:

- `@message`: the Russian sentence that names the channel (Channels::NotAvailable).
- `@back_url`: where «Вернуться в кабинет» goes.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="ru">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title><%= t('oauth_callback.channel_not_available.title', locale: :ru) %></title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
      body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
      main { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; max-width: 30rem; padding: 2rem 1rem; }
      h1 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.3; }
      p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
      a { display: inline-block; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 0.5rem; color: LinkText; text-decoration: none; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main role="main">
      <h1><%= t('oauth_callback.channel_not_available.title', locale: :ru) %></h1>
      <p id="channel-not-available-message"><%= @message %></p>
      <a href="<%= @back_url %>"><%= t('oauth_callback.channel_not_available.back', locale: :ru) %></a>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
